# REQUIRES: verilator
# --slr-group-cut (S26X, a32-S26X-C3): a value a group reads whose closure is
# past --slr-group-own's limit (at 32 SMs the frame sequencer's: it reads
# every memory port's tokens, so it grows with N) is not left in the level to
# fan out over the SLRs unregistered: the level computes it two host cycles
# ahead (its next-value logic applied twice), registers that (`<v>_lead`),
# and each reading group registers it again (`<v>_cut_g<g>`): one cone, both
# ends of every crossing registered, the same value in every host cycle.
# Here --slr-group-own 2 puts every closure past the limit (the sequencer's
# pos3, the decision's go): the same MATCH in exactly the host cycles of the
# replicated closures (--slr-group-own 1000), with stalls up to 90 %.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/late
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/own --static --nest --copies Leaf:3 --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --slr-groups --slr-region v80 --slr-assign Leaf:0,Leaf_copy1:1,Leaf_copy2:1,Top_model:2 --slr-group-control --slr-group-reset --slr-level 2 --slr-group-local 1000 --slr-group-own 1000 --slr-group-env Leaf > %t/own.log 2>&1
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/cut --static --nest --copies Leaf:3 --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --slr-groups --slr-region v80 --slr-assign Leaf:0,Leaf_copy1:1,Leaf_copy2:1,Top_model:2 --slr-group-control --slr-group-reset --slr-level 2 --slr-group-local 1000 --slr-group-own 2 --slr-group-cut --slr-group-env Leaf > %t/cut.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CUTLOG < %t/cut.log
# CUTLOG: slr-group-own: {{[0-9]+}} level registers and {{[0-9]+}} level ops replicated into groups, 0 closures left
# CUTLOG: slr-group-cut: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} values read by the groups from a lead-2 register ({{[0-9]+}} bits, {{[1-9][0-9]*}} group registers, {{[1-9][0-9]*}} lead ops in the level; {{[0-9]+}} level ops cloned into the groups before them)
# CUTLOG-NOT: warning: slr-group
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CUTSV < %t/cut/foldsim_sim.sv
# CUTSV-LABEL: module foldsim_sim_slr0(
# CUTSV: pos3_cut_g0 <= pos3_lead;
# CUTSV-LABEL: module foldsim_sim(
# CUTSV: pos3_lead <=
# The registers the leads read as they are and that also feed the groups (the
# reset's first stage) are read through copies of their own: every fanout over
# the SLRs is registers only (locality: no refusal; xcheck: no logic crossing).
# RUN: grep -q 'reset_pre_leadsrc <= hostReset' %t/cut/foldsim_sim.sv
# RUN: python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_locality.py %t/cut --out %t/cut/l > /dev/null
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LOC < %t/cut/l/locality.txt
# LOC: L3 global fanout
# LOC-NOT: REFUSE
# RUN: python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_xcheck.py %t/cut/foldsim_sim.mlir | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=X
# X: cross-group edges: {{.*}} LOGIC 0 (0 bits); group outputs read by the level: {{[0-9]+}}, LOGIC 0
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/own/obj %S/Inputs/tb_late.sv top.sv %t/own/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/own/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/cut/obj %S/Inputs/tb_late.sv top.sv %t/cut/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/cut/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/own/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=30 | grep MATCH > %t/own/r1.txt
# RUN: %t/own/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +stall=0 | grep MATCH > %t/own/r2.txt
# RUN: %t/own/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +stall=90 | grep MATCH > %t/own/r3.txt
# RUN: %t/cut/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=30 | grep MATCH > %t/cut/r1.txt
# RUN: %t/cut/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +stall=0 | grep MATCH > %t/cut/r2.txt
# RUN: %t/cut/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +stall=90 | grep MATCH > %t/cut/r3.txt
