# MUT: MISMATCH
# A lead that reaches a port within two register stages (--bubbles: the
# decision reads the kernel's `advance` as it is) is not built: the value stays
# in the level, said loudly, and the run is the same as without the option.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bub --static --nest --bubbles --copies Leaf:3 --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --slr-groups --slr-region v80 --slr-assign Leaf:0,Leaf_copy1:1,Leaf_copy2:1,Top_model:2 --slr-group-control --slr-group-reset --slr-level 2 --slr-group-local 1000 --slr-group-own 2 --slr-group-cut --slr-group-env Leaf > %t/bub.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BUB < %t/bub.log
# BUB: slr-group-cut: {{[0-9]+}} values read by the groups from a lead-2 register ({{.*}}), {{[1-9][0-9]*}} without a lead (read as they are: {{.*}}pos3{{.*}}; leaves: a port x{{[0-9]+}} (advance))
# BUB-NEXT: warning: slr-group-cut: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} values without a lead stay in the level
